  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Cast equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr has 8–16% room-temperature tensile ductility.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr has a yield strength of 163–530 MPa at 1000 °C at strain rates of 10^-4–10^-2 s^-1.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr has inadequate oxidation resistance for high-temperature use in air.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed intervention is incorporation of 2–4 at% Al into cast HfNbTaTiZr.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al-modified alloy can be synthesized by arc melting.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding 2–4 at% Al to HfNbTaTiZr will promote formation of a continuous protective alumina scale.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9787501::web::004::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting alumina scale will be adherent to the alloy surface.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Aluminum has a strong affinity for oxygen.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Minor Al additions will segregate to the HfNbTaTiZr surface during high-temperature exposure.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Surface-segregated Al will form Al2O3 in situ during exposure.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9787501::web::004::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A continuous Al2O3 scale will impede oxygen ingress and reduce further oxidation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9787501::web::004::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "After 5 hours in air at 800 °C, the Al-modified alloy will have lower oxidation weight gain than untreated equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9787501::web::004::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "After 5 hours in air at 800 °C, the Al-modified alloy will have better oxide-scale integrity than untreated equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9787501::web::004::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The 2–4 at% Al addition will largely preserve the room-temperature tensile ductility of HfNbTaTiZr.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9787501::web::004::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The 2–4 at% Al addition will largely preserve the 1000 °C yield strength of HfNbTaTiZr at strain rates of 10^-4–10^-2 s^-1.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9787501::web::004::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
